<title>BRAZIL: Brazil Ag Min maintains soybean, grains forecasts.</title>
<headline>Brazil Ag Min maintains soybean, grains forecasts.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1997-01-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's 1996/97 soybean crop should reach 25.70 million tonnes, midway in a range forecast in November of between 25.1 million and 25.91 million tonnes, said Brazil's Agriculture Minister.</p>
<p>&quot;We are still working on the basis of the previous, the first, CONAB estimate,&quot; Arlindo Porto told reporters.</p>
<p>CONAB is the Agriculture Ministry's National Supply Company.</p>
<p>The 1996/97 harvest represents a 10.8 percent rise on the previous crop of 23.19 million tonnes.</p>
<p>The ministry did the same with the total grains crop, estimating it at 77.56 million tonnes, midway between the previous forecast of 76.25 million to 78.53 million tonnes.</p>
<p>This is 5.4 percent on the previous harvest of 73.55 million tonnes.</p>
<p>-Michael Christie, Brasilia newsroom, 5561 2230358</p>
